sible maximums and minimums from each case and then determine the overall maximum and minimum.\n\n**Case 1 (4,1,1):**\n- Max: 210000\n- Min: 100002\n\n**Case 5 (2,2,2):**\n- Max: 221100\n- Min: 100122\n\n**Case 7 (1,4,1):**\n- Max: 211110\n- Min: 101112\n\n**Case 10 (1,1,4):**\n- Max: 222210\n- Min: 102222\n\nNow, let's collect all the maximums and minimums:\n\nMaximum candidates:\n- 210000 (Case 1)\n- 221100 (Case 5)\n- 211110 (Case 7)\n- 222210 (Case 10)\n\nMinimum candidates:\n- 100002 (Case 1)\n- 100122 (Case 5)\n- 101112 (Case 7)\n- 102222 (Case 10)\n\nNow, compare these to find the overall maximum and minimum.\n\n**Finding the Maximum:**\n\nLooking at the maximum candidates:\n\n- 210000\n- 221100\n- 211110\n- 222210\n\nComparing digit by digit:\n\n- 222210 is the largest since it starts with three 2s, whereas the others have lower digits earlier.\n\nBreakdown:\n\n- 222210 vs 221100: First three digits 222 vs 221 \u2192 222 is larger.\n- 222210 vs 211110: Clearly 222210 is larger.\n- 222210 vs 210000: Clearly larger.\n\nSo the overall maximum is 222210.\n\n**Finding the Minimum:**\n\nLooking at the minimum candidates:\n\n- 100002\n- 100122\n- 101112\n- 102222\n\nCompare digit by digit:\n\nAll start with 1, so look at the second digit:\n\n- 100002: Second digit 0\n- 100122: Second digit 0\n- 101112: Second digit 0\n- 102222: Second digit 0\n\nWait, all have 0 as the second digit? Wait:\n\nWait, 100002 is 1 0 0 0 0 2\n\n100122 is 1 0 0 1 2 2\n\n101112 is 1 0 1 1 1 2\n\n102222 is 1 0 2 2 2 2\n\nSo all start with 1 followed by 0. So compare the third digit:\n\n- 100002: third digit 0\n- 100122: third digit 0\n- 101112: third digit 1\n- 102222: third digit 2\n\nSo between the first two (100002 and 100122), third digit is 0 for both. Then compare the fourth digit:\n\n- 100002: fourth digit 0\n- 100122: fourth digit 1\n\nSo 100002 is smaller than 100122 because at the fourth digit, 0 < 1.\n\nNow compare 100002 with the others. The other numbers (101112 and 102222) are